        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "80e65af1-668f-5fff-8dd9-7c9e534b8232",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elizabeth Smylie, Vasek Pospisil, Jack Sock, Nicole Provis, Jo-Anne Faull, Julie Richardson, Bobby Reynolds, Pierre-Ludovic Duclos, Ivo Klec\n- Events: 1992 Dow Classic – Doubles, 2011 Jalisco Open – Doubles, 2014 Wimbledon Championships, 2015 Indian Wells Masters\n- Topics: professional tennis, Grand Slam titles, doubles, mixed doubles\n\nFacts:\n- Elizabeth Smylie, née Sayers and sometimes known as Liz Smylie, was born on 11 April 1963 and is a retired Australian professional tennis player.\n- Elizabeth Smylie won four Grand Slam titles during her career, including one in women's doubles and three in mixed doubles.\n- Vasek Pospisil and Bobby Reynolds won the first edition of the 2011 Jalisco Open doubles tournament by defeating Pierre-Ludovic Duclos and Ivo Klec 6–4, 6–7(6), [10–6] in the final.\n- Nicole Provis and Elizabeth Smylie were the defending champions in the 1992 Dow Classic doubles event, but Jo-Anne Faull and Julie Richardson defeated them in the quarterfinals.\n- Vasek Pospisil and Jack Sock won the men's doubles titles at the 2014 Wimbledon Championships and the 2015 Indian Wells Masters.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b9649307-e39a-519e-8192-730a331ed882",
        "text": "Page: Elizabeth Smylie. Sentence: Elizabeth Smylie (née Sayers, born 11 April 1963), sometimes known as Liz Smylie, is a retired Australian professional tennis player.\nPage: Elizabeth Smylie. Sentence: During her career, she won four Grand Slam titles, one of them in women's doubles and three in mixed doubles.\nPage: Vasek Pospisil. Sentence: Along with partner Jack Sock, he won the 2014 Wimbledon Championships and the 2015 Indian Wells Masters men's doubles titles.\nPage: 1992 Dow Classic – Doubles. Sentence: Nicole Provis and Elizabeth Smylie were the defending champions but were defeated in the quarterfinals by Jo-Anne Faull and Julie Richardson.\nPage: 2011 Jalisco Open – Doubles. Sentence: Vasek Pospisil and Bobby Reynolds won the first edition of this tournament, beating Pierre-Ludovic Duclos and Ivo Klec 6–4, 6–7(6), [10–6] in the final.",
